From: Codex <codex@openai.com>
Subject: [PATCH] label S9+ backlight for M4 SDHMS metadata reads

# Reason: M4 SDHMS logs `/sys/class/backlight/panel/brightness: fstat failed: EACCES` while Enforcing. The real node is panel_drv@001 and remains generic sysfs; an exact temporary label test using the already-authorized display type produced no new SDHMS fstat error in the observed interval. Existing policy grants system_app display getattr/read; no new allow is added.
# Affected: M4 vendor-restore hook, new exact-scope policy helper/lock, and real vendor ext4 image verifier. Add one genfscon for the exact brightness node; retain thermal values, thresholds, kernel and all other sysfs labels.
# Verify: helper positive/idempotence and duplicate/conflicting/missing-permission fixtures; Python/shell syntax; require the exact CIL rule and existing permission in the final vendor image, checking image bytes/mode/owner/label. Device restorecon/reboot and SDHMS log verification remain a required runtime gate.
# Rollback: reverse this patch and rebuild the M4 candidate; no current release artifact or protected device partition is changed by this source patch.

